        "original_id": "2bfc5c87-76e8-5f1b-9589-2b9afe712d4e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Felipe Calderón\n- Places: La Yesca Dam, Grande de Santiago River, Barranca de Oblatos, Jalisco, Mexico\n- Topics: dam inaugurations, dam completion, Mexican presidency\n\nFacts:\n- Felipe Calderón was born on 18 August 1962.\n- Felipe Calderón served as President of Mexico from 1 December 2006 to 30 November 2012.\n- The El Cajón Dam downstream on the Grande de Santiago River was completed in 2007.\n- La Yesca Dam on the Grande de Santiago River was completed in 2012.\n- President Felipe Calderón inaugurated La Yesca Dam on 6 November 2012.\n- Barranca de Oblatos, also known as Barranca de Huentitán, is a canyon in Jalisco, Mexico, carved by the Río Grande de Santiago.",
